<p>Asha Leena Bhandary, recently professor of philosophy at University of Iowa, has moved to Stony Brook University.<span id="more-58254"></span></p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="wp-image-58256 aligncenter" src="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/bhandary.jpg" alt="" width="305" height="305" srcset="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/bhandary.jpg 768w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/bhandary-300x300.jpg 300w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/bhandary-150x150.jpg 150w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/bhandary-400x400.jpg 400w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/bhandary-177x177.jpg 177w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/bhandary-380x380.jpg 380w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 305px) 100vw, 305px" /></p>
<p><a href="https://www.ashabhandary.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Professor Bhandary</a> works in social and political philosophy, ethics, feminist theory, and philosophy of race. She is the author of <em>Freedom to Care: Liberalism, Dependency Care, and Culture</em> (2020) and <em>Being at Home: Living Autonomously in an Unjust World </em>(2026), among other works, which you can learn more about <a href="https://www.ashabhandary.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a> and <a href="https://philpapers.org/s/Asha%20Leena%20Bhandary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a>.</p>
<p>At Stony Brook, Professor Bhandary will have a joint appointment at the university&#8217;s <a href="https://renaissance.stonybrookmedicine.edu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">School of Medicine</a> (as Professor and Vice Chair of Care Ethics Research in the Department of Family, Population and Preventive Medicine and the Center for Medical Humanities, Compassionate Care and Bioethics) and the <a href="https://www.stonybrook.edu/philosophy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Department of Philosophy</a> (as Professor).</p>
<p>She officially takes up her position at Stony Brook tomorrow.</p><p>The post <a href="https://dailynous.com/2026/08/31/bhandary-from-iowa-to-stony-brook/">Bhandary from Iowa to Stony Brook</a> first appeared on <a href="https://dailynous.com">Daily Nous</a>.</p>